  (typeof ngDevMode === "undefined" || ngDevMode) && i055.\u0275setClassMetadata(AcronisOtContentComponent, [{
    type: Component55,
    args: [{ selector: "xh-acronis-ot-content", standalone: true, changeDetection: ChangeDetectionStrategy55.OnPush, template: '<section class="ot-matters" aria-labelledby="otMattersTitle">\r\n  <header class="ot-heading">\r\n    <span>Why it matters</span>\r\n    <h2 id="otMattersTitle">The OT protection choice of automation vendors</h2>\r\n    <p>Trusted across automotive, chemicals, oil &amp; gas, power, pharma, steel and logistics at Global-2000<br />enterprises \u2014 and delivered locally by XcellHost.</p>\r\n  </header>\r\n\r\n  <div class="ot-grid ot-grid-four">\r\n    <article class="ot-card">\r\n      <span class="ot-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><path d="M12 6v6l4 2"/></svg></span>\r\n      <h3>Every OT OS \u2014 XP era to today</h3>\r\n      <p>Backup and recovery even for older Windows and Linux that other vendors have abandoned \u2014 keeping legacy plant systems protected.</p>\r\n    </article>\r\n    <article class="ot-card">\r\n      <span class="ot-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 2l8 3v6c0 5.5-3.5 9.7-8 11-4.5-1.3-8-5.5-8-11V5l8-3z"/><path d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"/></svg></span>\r\n      <h3>Air-gapped environments</h3>\r\n      <p>Keeps OT systems protected even where there are no external network connections, for security-isolated plant floors.</p>\r\n    </article>\r\n    <article class="ot-card">\r\n      <span class="ot-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M23 4v6h-6M1 20v-6h6"/><path d="M3.5 9a9 9 0 0115-3.4L23 10M1 14l4.5 4.4A9 9 0 0020.5 15"/></svg></span>\r\n      <h3>Local recovery, no IT needed</h3>\r\n      <p>One-Click Recovery lets workers with no IT skills restore a failed OT system in minutes \u2014 no waiting for IT staff.</p>\r\n    </article>\r\n    <article class="ot-card">\r\n      <span class="ot-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M14 2H6a2 2 0 00-2 2v16a2 2 0 002 2h12a2 2 0 002-2V8l-6-6z"/><path d="M14 2v6h6M8 13h8M8 17h8"/></svg></span>\r\n      <h3>Regulatory compliance</h3>\r\n      <p>Secure, compliant backup and recovery that helps meet IEC 62443, NERC-CIP and GxP \u2014 and India\u2019s DPDP.</p>\r\n    </article>\r\n  </div>\r\n</section>\r\n\r\n<section class="ot-proof" aria-labelledby="otProofTitle">\r\n  <div class="ot-inner">\r\n    <header class="ot-heading"><span>Proof</span><h2 id="otProofTitle">Why industry leaders choose it for OT resilience</h2><p>Representative outcomes from Global-2000 OT and ICS operators. *As reported by Acronis.</p></header>\r\n    <div class="ot-proof-grid">\r\n      <article><strong>50\xD7</strong><small>protected workloads</small><h3>Tata Steel</h3><p>Modernised backup infrastructure, taking control of critical data and scaling protected workloads 50-fold.</p></article>\r\n      <article><strong>30% / 12%</strong><small>CapEx / OpEx cut</small><h3>BDR Pharmaceuticals</h3><p>Faster, more efficient, secure backup with complete dashboard visibility of backup and restore.</p></article>\r\n      <article><strong>Seconds</strong><small>to restore any system</small><h3>ABB</h3><p>Customers avoid costly business interruptions by restoring the functions of any system in seconds.</p></article>\r\n      <article><strong>Zero</strong><small>compatibility issues</small><h3>Sasol</h3><p>Reliable restore to dissimilar hardware, seamless virtual\u2194physical migration and stringent compliance met.</p></article>\r\n    </div>\r\n  </div>\r\n</section>\r\n\r\n<section class="ot-how" aria-labelledby="otHowTitle">\r\n  <header class="ot-heading"><span>How it works</span><h2 id="otHowTitle">Back up live OT systems. Recover in minutes.</h2><p>Agent-based, image-based, air-gap-friendly \u2014 managed by XcellHost.</p></header>\r\n  <div class="ot-step-grid">\r\n    <article><strong>01</strong><span class="ot-step-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><rect x="2" y="2" width="20" height="8" rx="2"/><rect x="2" y="14" width="20" height="8" rx="2"/><path d="M6 6h.01M6 18h.01"/></svg></span><h3>Agent, no downtime</h3><p>Install the agent on a live OT system \u2014 no reboot, no scheduled production downtime, even at first install.</p></article>\r\n    <article><strong>02</strong><span class="ot-step-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M23 4v6h-6M1 20v-6h6"/><path d="M3.5 9a9 9 0 0115-3.4L23 10M1 14l4.5 4.4A9 9 0 0020.5 15"/></svg></span><h3>Image backup daily</h3><p>Automated image-based backups (multiple times a day to monthly), or triggered on reboot or a failing drive.</p></article>\r\n    <article><strong>03</strong><span class="ot-step-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 2l8 3v6c0 5.5-3.5 9.7-8 11-4.5-1.3-8-5.5-8-11V5l8-3z"/><path d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"/></svg></span><h3>3-2-1, air-gapped</h3><p>Keep 3 copies on 2 media with 1 off-site \u2014 local, NAS/SAN, tape or India cloud, immutable and encrypted.</p></article>\r\n    <article><strong>04</strong><span class="ot-step-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M13 2L3 14h7l-1 8 10-12h-7l1-8z"/></svg></span><h3>One-click restore</h3><p>A failed system is restored in minutes by local staff, or to new hardware via Universal Restore.</p></article>\r\n  </div>\r\n</section>\r\n\r\n<section class="ot-coverage" aria-labelledby="otCoverageTitle">\r\n  <header class="ot-heading"><span>Coverage</span><h2 id="otCoverageTitle">Industry-best OS, hypervisor and storage support</h2><p>Unique, ongoing support for legacy systems other vendors have abandoned \u2014 so the oldest plant<br />systems stay protected.</p></header>\r\n  <div class="ot-coverage-grid">\r\n    <article>\r\n      <div class="ot-coverage-title"><span class="ot-coverage-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M3 4.5 11 3v8H3V4.5ZM13 2.7 21 1v10h-8V2.7ZM3 13h8v8l-8-1.5V13ZM13 13h8v10l-8-1.7V13Z"/></svg></span><h3>Windows</h3></div>\r\n      <p>Server 2003\u20132022, XP\u2013Windows 11, Small Business &amp; Storage Server</p>\r\n    </article>\r\n    <article>\r\n      <div class="ot-coverage-title"><span class="ot-coverage-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><rect x="2.5" y="4" width="19" height="16" rx="2"/><path d="m6 9 3 3-3 3M11 16h6"/></svg></span><h3>Linux</h3></div>\r\n      <p>Kernel 2.6.9\u20135.19 \xB7 RHEL, Ubuntu, SUSE, Debian, CentOS, Oracle, Alma, Rocky</p>\r\n    </article>\r\n    <article>\r\n      <div class="ot-coverage-title"><span class="ot-coverage-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><rect x="3" y="3" width="18" height="7" rx="1.5"/><rect x="3" y="14" width="8" height="7" rx="1.5"/><rect x="13" y="14" width="8" height="7" rx="1.5"/><path d="M12 10v2M7 12h10M7 12v2M17 12v2"/></svg></span><h3>Hypervisors</h3></div>\r\n      <p>VMware vSphere 4.1\u20138.0, Hyper-V, Citrix, KVM, RHEV, Nutanix AHV, Virtuozzo, Scale</p>\r\n    </article>\r\n    <article>\r\n      <div class="ot-coverage-title"><span class="ot-coverage-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><rect x="3" y="3" width="18" height="18" rx="2"/><path d="M3 9h18M9 9v12M14 14h4M16 12v4"/></svg></span><h3>Applications</h3></div>\r\n      <p>Microsoft Exchange 2007\u20132019 \xB7 SQL Server 2005\u20132022</p>\r\n    </article>\r\n    <article>\r\n      <div class="ot-coverage-title"><span class="ot-coverage-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><rect x="4" y="3" width="16" height="13" rx="2"/><path d="M2 19h20l-2 2H4l-2-2ZM10 16v3M14 16v3"/></svg></span><h3>macOS</h3></div>\r\n      <p>OS X 10.9 \u2192 macOS Sonoma 14</p>\r\n    </article>\r\n    <article>\r\n      <div class="ot-coverage-title"><span class="ot-coverage-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><ellipse cx="12" cy="5" rx="9" ry="3"/><path d="M3 5v7c0 1.7 4 3 9 3s9-1.3 9-3V5M3 12v7c0 1.7 4 3 9 3s9-1.3 9-3v-7"/></svg></span><h3>Storage</h3></div>\r\n      <p>Local disk, NAS, SAN, private/public cloud, Acronis &amp; XcellHost cloud, tape</p>\r\n    </article>\r\n  </div>\r\n</section>\r\n\r\n<section class="ot-purdue" aria-labelledby="otPurdueTitle">\r\n  <div class="ot-inner">\r\n    <header class="ot-heading ot-heading-dark">\r\n      <span>Purdue Reference Model</span>\r\n      <h2 id="otPurdueTitle">Protection mapped to your OT architecture</h2>\r\n      <p>Acronis protects OT at Purdue Levels 2, 3 and 3.5 \u2014 and many manufacturers also protect IT systems<br />at Levels 4 and 5.</p>\r\n    </header>\r\n\r\n    <div class="ot-purdue-grid">\r\n      <article style="--level-color: #a78bfa"><i></i><h3>Level 3.5 \u2014 IT/OT DMZ</h3><p>Patch servers, historian mirrors</p></article>\r\n      <article style="--level-color: #ffb15c"><i></i><h3>Level 3 \u2014 Operations</h3><p>Historians, I/O servers</p></article>\r\n      <article style="--level-color: #4ade80"><i></i><h3>Level 2 \u2014 Supervisory control</h3><p>SCADA, HMI, jump servers</p></article>\r\n      <article style="--level-color: #8ab4ff"><i></i><h3>Levels 4 &amp; 5 \u2014 Enterprise IT</h3><p>ERP, business networks (also protected)</p></article>\r\n    </div>\r\n  </div>\r\n</section>\r\n\r\n<section class="ot-advanced" aria-labelledby="otAdvancedTitle">\r\n  <header class="ot-heading">\r\n    <span>Advanced features</span>\r\n    <h2 id="otAdvancedTitle">One agent for OT resilience and cybersecurity</h2>\r\n  </header>\r\n\r\n  <div class="ot-grid ot-grid-three">\r\n    <article class="ot-card">\r\n      <span class="ot-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 2l8 3v6c0 5.5-3.5 9.7-8 11-4.5-1.3-8-5.5-8-11V5l8-3z"/><path d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"/></svg></span>\r\n      <h3>Integrated security + backup</h3>\r\n      <p>The same agent adds Active Protection against ransomware, antivirus/anti-malware, drive-health monitoring and EDR \u2014 backups are scanned and remediated before restore.</p>\r\n    </article>\r\n    <article class="ot-card">\r\n      <span class="ot-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 2l10 5-10 5L2 7l10-5z"/><path d="M2 12l10 5 10-5M2 17l10 5 10-5"/></svg></span>\r\n      <h3>Front- &amp; back-office too</h3>\r\n      <p>Protect systems beyond the plant floor \u2014 ERP, supply chain, procurement, QC, maintenance, finance, HR, sales, marketing and support.</p>\r\n    </article>\r\n    <article class="ot-card">\r\n      <span class="ot-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M17.5 19a4.5 4.5 0 000-9 6 6 0 00-11.6 1.5A3.8 3.8 0 006.5 19h11z"/></svg></span>\r\n      <h3>Cloud-based protections</h3>\r\n      <p>Add cloud Management Servers for disaster recovery, Microsoft 365 / Google Workspace protection and secure off-site backup storage.</p>\r\n    </article>\r\n    <article class="ot-card">\r\n      <span class="ot-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M1 12s4-7 11-7 11 7 11 7-4 7-11 7-11-7-11-7z"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3"/></svg></span>\r\n      <h3>Centralised dashboard</h3>\r\n      <p>Stream OT metadata to a central warehouse and Monitoring Hub, with third-party monitoring, reporting and analytics.</p>\r\n    </article>\r\n    <article class="ot-card">\r\n      <span class="ot-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3"/><path d="M19.4 15a1.65 1.65 0 00.33 1.82l.06.06a2 2 0 11-2.83 2.83l-.06-.06a1.65 1.65 0 00-1.82-.33 1.65 1.65 0 00-1 1.51V21a2 2 0 01-4 0v-.09A1.65 1.65 0 009 19.4a1.65 1.65 0 00-1.82.33l-.06.06a2 2 0 11-2.83-2.83l.06-.06a1.65 1.65 0 00.33-1.82A1.65 1.65 0 003.17 14H3a2 2 0 010-4h.09A1.65 1.65 0 004.6 9a1.65 1.65 0 00-.33-1.82l-.06-.06a2 2 0 112.83-2.83l.06.06A1.65 1.65 0 009 4.6h.08A1.65 1.65 0 0010 3.09V3a2 2 0 014 0v.09a1.65 1.65 0 001 1.51 1.65 1.65 0 001.82-.33l.06-.06a2 2 0 112.83 2.83l-.06.06a1.65 1.65 0 00-.33 1.82V9a1.65 1.65 0 001.51 1H21a2 2 0 010 4h-.09A1.65 1.65 0 0019.4 15z"/></svg></span>\r\n      <h3>Management &amp; forensics</h3>\r\n      <p>Vulnerability assessment, patch management and hardware/software inventory \u2014 plus forensic backups for post-incident investigation and compliance.</p>\r\n    </article>\r\n    <article class="ot-card">\r\n      <span class="ot-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M23 4v6h-6M1 20v-6h6"/><path d="M3.5 9a9 9 0 0115-3.4L23 10M1 14l4.5 4.4A9 9 0 0020.5 15"/></svg></